Organon is not under a single licence, and this file exists so that nothing —
a tool, a sidebar badge, or a person in a hurry — can conclude otherwise.

  The engine crates                          MIT OR Apache-2.0
    native/organon-core                      (licensee's choice of either)
    native/organon-render
    native/organon-mind
    native/organon-console
    native/xtask

  The root crate                             GPL-3.0-or-later
    native/  (the VST3/CLAP plugin, the standalone,
              the visual, the `organon` CLI)

The split is forced, not chosen. The root crate calls nih-plug's
`nih_export_vst3!`, which is implemented over `vst3-sys`, which is GPLv3 — so
anything built from the root crate must be distributable under the GPL. nih-plug
itself is ISC and CLAP is MIT/Apache-2.0; only the VST3 arm carries the
obligation. Collapsing the two "for consistency" would relicense roughly 100,000
lines of reusable engine onto the terms of a plugin binding, which is the
opposite of the intent.

Full texts, all three, in this directory:

  LICENSE-MIT      the MIT licence
  LICENSE-APACHE   the Apache Licence 2.0
  LICENSE-GPL      the GNU General Public License v3

LICENSING.md explains which terms reach which artifact, and why, in more detail
than fits here. Read it before changing any crate's `license` field.

Third-party code carries its own terms alongside its own source: see NOTICE, and
the LICENSE files under native/vendor/.

A licence grants copyright, not trademark. The Organon name and brand remain the
author's.
